<% settings = @reference.settings %>
<% endpoint = @reference.endpoint_url %>
<% metadata_path = "/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource#{settings.endpoint_path}" %>
<% max_mib = McpEndpoint::MAX_REQUEST_BYTES / 1.megabyte %>

<header class="masthead">
  <div class="wide">
    <p class="server"><%= settings.server_title %>, version <%= settings.server_version %></p>
    <h1>POST <%= endpoint %></h1>
    <p class="lede">This server lets AI clients read and change posts and their comments through the Model Context Protocol. Every request is one self-contained HTTP call with an OAuth token.</p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Transport</dt>
      <dd>Streamable HTTP, stateless: one JSON response per request, with no sessions or streams</dd>
      <dt>Protocol</dt>
      <dd><%= @reference.protocol_versions.join(", ") %></dd>
      <dt>Sign-in</dt>
      <dd>OAuth 2.1 with PKCE. Discovery starts at <a href="<%= metadata_path %>"><code><%= metadata_path %></code></a></dd>
      <dt>Contract</dt>
      <dd><a href="<%= docs_tools_path %>"><code><%= docs_tools_path %></code></a>, the exact <code>tools/list</code> result</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wide page">
  <nav aria-label="On this page">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#connect">Connect a client</a></li>
      <li><a href="#call">How a call travels</a></li>
      <li><a href="#token">How a client gets a token</a></li>
      <li>
        <a href="#tools">Tools</a>
        <ul>
          <% @reference.tools.each do |tool| %>
            <li><a href="#<%= tool.tool_name %>"><%= tool.tool_name %></a></li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><a href="#scopes">Scopes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#ownership">Who owns what</a></li>
      <li><a href="#errors">Errors</a></li>
      <li><a href="#http">Raw HTTP</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <section id="connect">
      <h2>Connect a client</h2>
      <p>Give any MCP client the URL. It finds the sign-in server by itself and opens a browser for you to approve it.</p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code><%= endpoint %></code></pre>
      <p>To browse the tools and call them by hand, use the <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/tools/inspector">MCP Inspector</a>. It is to MCP what Swagger UI is to REST, and needs Node 22.19 or newer.</p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector@<%= DocsHelper::INSPECTOR_VERSION %> \
  --server-url <%= endpoint %> --transport http</code></pre>
      <% if Rails.env.development? %>
        <p class="note">Sign in with <code>SEED_USER_EMAIL</code> and <code>SEED_USER_PASSWORD</code> from your <code>.env</code> file.</p>
      <% end %>
      <p class="note">MCP has no OpenAPI-style file: a client reads the contract live from <code>tools/list</code>. This page and the contract link above are built from the same classes that answer that call, so they cannot disagree with it.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="call">
      <h2>How a call travels</h2>
      <p>One <code>get_post</code> call, from the client to the database and back. The circles are checks. Coral text says how each check refuses a request, and the <a href="#errors">errors table</a> says what a client does about it.</p>
      <%= render "sequence", sequence: DocsHelper::TOOL_CALL %>
      <dl class="key">
        <dt>Rails</dt><dd><code>config/environments/production.rb</code>, <code>config/initializers/rack_attack.rb</code></dd>
        <dt>Transport</dt><dd><code>app/mcp/mcp_endpoint.rb</code>, <code>app/mcp/doorkeeper_token_verifier.rb</code> and the SDK</dd>
        <dt>Tool</dt><dd><code>app/mcp/application_tool.rb</code>, <code>app/mcp/posts/*_tool.rb</code>, <code>app/mcp/comments/*_tool.rb</code></dd>
        <dt>Interaction</dt><dd><code>app/interactions/posts/*.rb</code>, <code>app/interactions/comments/*.rb</code>, which the REST API uses too</dd>
        <dt>Post</dt><dd><code>app/models/post.rb</code></dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section id="token">
      <h2>How a client gets a token</h2>
      <p>The first connection asks for every scope, so one consent covers every tool.</p>
      <%= render "sequence", sequence: DocsHelper::FIRST_CONNECTION %>
      <p>A client that holds too little, because it asked for less or connected before a new tool was added, gets a <code>403</code> naming the scope, and asks the person once more.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="tools">
      <h2>Tools</h2>
      <div class="table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All tools">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Scope</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <% @reference.tools.each do |tool| %>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="#<%= tool.tool_name %>"><code><%= tool.tool_name %></code></a></td>
                <td><span class="<%= scope_class(tool.required_scope) %>"><%= tool.required_scope %></span></td>
                <td><%= @reference.behavior(tool) %></td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Every tool returns its result twice, as <code>structuredContent</code> and as the same JSON in <code>content[0].text</code>, for clients that do not read structured content yet. The server also tells clients that titles and bodies are data, never instructions to follow.</p>

      <% @reference.tools.each do |tool| %>
        <%= render "tool", tool:, reference: @reference %>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section id="scopes">
      <h2>Scopes</h2>
      <div class="table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All scopes">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>The consent page says</th><th>Tools</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <% @reference.scopes.each do |scope| %>
              <tr>
                <td><code><%= scope %></code></td>
                <td><%= @reference.scope_label(scope) %></td>
                <td>
                  <% @reference.tools_with_scope(scope).each do |tool| %>
                    <a href="#<%= tool.tool_name %>"><code><%= tool.tool_name %></code></a>
                  <% end %>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="ownership">
      <h2>Who owns what</h2>
      <p>Whoever approves a client is the user it acts for. The server reads that user from the token, never from tool arguments, so a client cannot claim to be someone else.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Every signed-in user can read every post and comment, and add comments to any post. <code>mine</code> says which records are yours, and <code>list_posts</code> takes <code>mine: true</code> to show only those.</li>
        <li>Only the owner can update or delete a record. Deleting a post also deletes the comments of other users on it.</li>
        <li>Scopes say what a client may do. Ownership says to which records.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="errors">
      <h2>Errors</h2>
      <p>Refusals are HTTP errors. A tool that ran but could not do its job answers <code>200</code> with <code>isError</code>, so that the model can read why and decide what to do next.</p>
      <div class="table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All errors">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Response</th><th>When</th><th>What the client does</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td class="wrap">The request has no token.</td><td class="wrap">Starts sign-in from the <code>resource_metadata</code> URL in <code>WWW-Authenticate</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>401</code> <code>invalid_token</code></td><td class="wrap">The token is unknown, expired, revoked or issued for another server. All four get the same answer.</td><td class="wrap">Refreshes it, or signs in again.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>400</code> <code>invalid_request</code></td><td class="wrap">The <code>Authorization</code> header is not one Bearer token.</td><td class="wrap">Fixes the header.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>403</code> <code>insufficient_scope</code></td><td class="wrap">The token lacks the scope of this tool. <code>WWW-Authenticate</code> names it.</td><td class="wrap">Asks the person again, for the scopes it has plus that one.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>403</code> <code>-32600</code></td><td class="wrap">The Origin or Host is not allowed.</td><td class="wrap">A browser client needs its origin in <code>MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS</code>. Other clients send no Origin.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>405</code></td><td class="wrap"><code>GET /mcp</code>: this server offers no event stream.</td><td class="wrap">Uses <code>POST</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>413</code></td><td class="wrap">The body is over <%= max_mib %> MiB.</td><td class="wrap">Sends less.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>429</code></td><td class="wrap">Too many requests from this address or token.</td><td class="wrap">Waits for <code>Retry-After</code> seconds.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>400</code> <code>-32700</code></td><td class="wrap">The body is not valid JSON.</td><td class="wrap">Fixes the request.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>200</code> <code>-32602</code></td><td class="wrap">No tool has that name.</td><td class="wrap">Lists the tools again.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>200</code> <code>-32603</code></td><td class="wrap">The server failed unexpectedly. The message holds no details, and the failure is reported on the server.</td><td class="wrap">Retries later.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>200</code> <code>isError</code></td><td class="wrap">Arguments do not match the input schema. The text says which.</td><td class="wrap">Corrects the call.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>200</code> <code>isError</code> <code>not_found</code></td><td class="wrap">The record does not exist. Someone may have deleted it since the client read it.</td><td class="wrap">Stops using this id, and lists what exists now or tells the person.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>200</code> <code>isError</code> <code>not_owner</code></td><td class="wrap">The record belongs to another user.</td><td class="wrap">Does not retry, and tells the person.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>200</code> <code>isError</code> <code>validation_failed</code></td><td class="wrap">Values were refused. <code>fields</code> lists them.</td><td class="wrap">Corrects them and calls again.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>The last three carry a code, a message and the next step as JSON in the text of the result. Here, a model comments on a post that its owner has just deleted:</p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code><%= JSON.pretty_generate(error: { code: "not_found", message: "Post 5 does not exist. It may have been deleted since you last read it.", next_step: "Do not retry with this id. Call list_posts to see what exists now, or tell the user it is gone." }) %></code></pre>
    </section>

    <section id="http">
      <h2>Raw HTTP</h2>
      <p>Clients handle all of this for you, but it helps to see one call. In development, get a one-hour token with all scopes:</p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>TOKEN=$(docker compose exec -T web bin/rails mcp:dev_token)</code></pre>
      <p>Then call a tool:</p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>curl <%= endpoint %> \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Accept: application/json, text/event-stream" \
  -H "MCP-Protocol-Version: 2025-11-25" \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"get_post","arguments":{"id":1}}}'</code></pre>
      <p>The response:</p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code><%= JSON.pretty_generate(jsonrpc: "2.0", id: 1, result: { content: [ { type: "text", text: Posts::ToolPayload::EXAMPLE.to_json } ], isError: false, structuredContent: Posts::ToolPayload::EXAMPLE }) %></code></pre>
      <details>
        <summary>The same call on protocol 2026-07-28</summary>
        <p>This version has no <code>initialize</code> handshake. Each request carries its own protocol version and client details, and repeats the method and tool name as headers.</p>
        <pre tabindex="0"><code>curl <%= endpoint %> \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Accept: application/json, text/event-stream" \
  -H "MCP-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28" \
  -H "Mcp-Method: tools/call" \
  -H "Mcp-Name: get_post" \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"get_post","arguments":{"id":1},"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion":"2026-07-28","io.modelcontextprotocol/clientInfo":{"name":"curl","version":"1.0"},"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities":{}}}}'</code></pre>
      </details>
    </section>
  </main>
</div>

<footer>
  <div class="wide">This page is rendered from the tool classes in <code>app/mcp</code> on every request.</div>
</footer>
